P11 (the landing page) is done. The earlier session had already written the code in the last commit, `efde87b`. I checked that code against premium §6.1 and found nothing missing, so this session only verified it, ticked P11 in `tasks.md` and added the P11 entry to `logs/progress.md`.

**What the landing now has (premium §6.1):**
- **Hero:** centred from 1024 px wide and left-aligned below that, with a 64 px headline between 640 and 1279 px.
- **Buttons:** "Open the sample lot" is the only filled button on the page, next to a secondary "Open file".
- **Hint line:** under the buttons, with a shorter version on mobile.
- **Sample cards:** each card is one button with its wafer disc, contact shadow and sheen. Disc sizes are 152, 140, 120 and 112 px by breakpoint.
- **Card layout:** three across from 1024 px, stacked 160 px rows at sm, and a swipeable row at 390 px where the second card peeks 46 px.
- **Footer:** "Runs entirely in your browser." on the left and "Download sample files" on the right.
- **Copy:** the new text is in all 5 locales.

**Verification:**
- `pnpm typecheck` and `pnpm lint` are clean, and `pnpm test` passes 276/276.
- After a fresh build, 28/28 e2e tests passed across 8 specs: `landing-p11` (covers A14 and A20 at 1440, 1280, 1024, 800 and 390, in light and dark), `landing-r4`, `scaffold`, `typography-p4`, `disc-material-p5`, `die-tiles-p6`, `stage-shadows-p7` and `vertical-slice`.
- In `perf-gate`, only the known frame-timing check failed; its other two tests passed.
- No visual snapshots changed.

**Decisions logged in progress.md:**
- §6.1 gives no disc size for the 390 px card, so it reuses the 112 px sm disc.
- The parse-error and no-results screens keep their old layout until P14.

